"The Israelites had spent no less than thirty-eight years in coming from Kadesh-Barnea to their encampment north of Zared. Here, at this fortieth station, they were commanded to pass through Moab by re Ar, the chief city; but were not to stop till they came to the valley on the south of Arnon.  At this last station but one they probably continued no longer than was necessary for sending messengers to Sihon, king of the Amorites, at Heshbon, and receiving his answer.  They then crossed the Arnon; and having vanquished Sihon and Og, took possession of the forty-second and last encampment. 

